'''Hurricane Amara''' ({{langx|bl|Sulcarano Amara|lit=bitter blowing storm}}; international designation: '''1224''', [[Balisca Meteorological Agency|BMA]] designation: '''16A''') was an extraordinarily rare {{W|South Atlantic tropical cyclone}}, and one of ## recorded hurricane strength storms on record in the {{W|South Atlantic Ocean}}. As of 2025, it is the most intense [[W:tropical cyclone|tropical cyclones]] to hit Balisca. ''Amara'' made landfall near [[Jatiel]], [[Araucaria]] at peak intensity, with the equivalent of {{W|Saffir–Simpson scale#Category 4|Category 4}} hurricane-force sustained winds. ''Amara'' was the first major hurricanes to hit the [[Baliscan archipelago]].

